From 47bb81abda6008f8df93286393a7995f4420bc28 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ruscher <rruscher@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 02:50:15 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 68/73] apps: Gives wlmcalclock preferences: Themes, analog
 clock, and more.

wlmcalclock reads its preferences file, and applies changes right away:
- Theme: The shared color themes, or its own colors.
- ClockStyle: Digital, or Analog: A clock face on the whole icon, with the
  weekday and a date window.
- TwelveHour, Seconds: As the commandline options, which remain defaults.
- BlinkColon: The colon blinks, every second.
- CalendarStyle: A sheet of paper, or a digital display.
- ShowYear: The year next to the month.
- TimeZone: Local, or a zone name like America/Sao_Paulo.
- CalendarCommand: Runs on a left click, eg. a calendar program.

Weekday and month names still follow the locale.
